  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. Aarav wants to change his flight from ATL to PHL to the cheapest Economy cabin flight the day after the original reservation. First, I need to find out the details of his current reservation. The user ID is aarav_garcia_1177, and the reservations listed are M05KNL and UHDAHF. I should check both to see which one is the relevant one for the ATL to PHL trip.\n\nSo, I'll start by using the get_reservation_details function for reservation M05KNL. If that's not the right one, I'll check UHDAHF. Once I have the reservation details, I can see the original flight date and then look for flights on the next day. Since he wants the cheapest Economy cabin, I need to search for flights on the following day and pick the cheapest one. Also, since he's a gold member, he gets more free checked bags, but he might not need that info right now. The payment method is covered by the original payment for refund, so I need to handle the payment part when modifying the reservation. Let's get the reservation details first.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_reservation_details\", \"arguments\": {\"reservation_id\": \"M05KNL\"}}\n",
